<title>BELGIUM: Belgian yr/yr inflation 2.31 pct in January.</title>
<headline>Belgian yr/yr inflation 2.31 pct in January.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian Economic Affairs Ministry released the following data on inflation -</p>
<p>    BELGIAN CONSUMER PRICES	Jan	  Dec	 Jan 1996</p>
<p>    Index (base 100=1988)	 124.65     123.79     121.84</p>
<p>    Mth/mth change (in pct)	 0.69	 0.18	 0.91</p>
<p>    Yr/yr change (in pct)	   2.31	 2.53	 1.96</p>
<p>(file take 1 FIRST, then fill out the rest of the table)</p>
<p>    Health index *		  122.09     121.29</p>
<p>    Mth/mth change (in pct)	 0.66	 0.14</p>
<p>NOTE - * excludes unhealthy products such as tobacco, alcohol and petrol, is used for inflation adjustments of rents and wages.</p>
<p>The ministry said price rises were mainly seen for foreign travel, fresh vegetables and petrol, while lower prices were recorded for holiday villages.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
